{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update8.json\",\"summary\":\"Bound the completed ballot-progress receipt 911d45335b3047178a6fd739f24b2cfb (fixed experiment adfa9c6d31ca481896e5ca1277f6cdf4-experiment, exit 0, 36 events, no parsing errors) into the authority question. Both declared non-leader comparisons are violated with complete witnesses 20 and 25: across two retry rounds the owner tried the identical ballot 0 while every answering peer reported the stored ballot 7, so appended_replies stayed at its own self reply out of a slow quorum of 3, no sub-case was dispatched, no follow-up message was emitted and the instance stayed accepted but uncommitted; the two control comparisons hold (evaluated 31 and 32), where the target's own BeTheLeader authority produced ballot 10, matching replies, the accept dispatch and a committed X at replicas 0, 1, 3 and 4. The question's discrimination is answered, so its disposition is set to explained, and the two supporting behaviors now cite the executed indices. Counterevidence and limits are recorded: replicas whose fixed ballot is above the stored one are not blocked by this mechanism, the peer rejections are legitimate answers, the premise came from a permitted failure of a recovery attempt after its Prepare broadcast, and the recoverer here is the owner - the extreme case whose fixed ballot is 0. Remaining unfinished work: the separate lead about the recovered commit's Seq, and any non-owner recoverer case.\"}"}}
